  "sourceFacts": {
    "horizontalBasis": "The earlier reference-only record had no mapped geometry or direction. Current PMTiles whole35184421893277 and its same-ID multilingual POI Monza Cathedral/Duomo di Monza identify the main footprint at the retained reference anchor. Northwest tall campanile,western Piazza del Duomo and photographs sign the western front. Heading0.06016824725424221 rad derives from the whole western edge;no exact Wikidata-tagged way match is asserted. All124 raw points/properties in16 current whole/part controls retained without horizontal rescale.",
    "architecturalHeights": "Raw low-body18 m,main roof27 m,full front28 m,middle front32 m,central front36 m and facade pinnacles27/35/40 m are retained. Interpret these as lower eave18 m,main ridge27 m,stepped facade envelope and respective pinnacle tips. Raw campanile62 m,inner crown72 m and lantern75 m fix the staged envelope;lower shaft50 m,belfry50..62 m,pediments66.5 m,cap72 m and lantern75 m are picture-led partitions,with an estimated79 m final finial. Crossing35 m part controls the green hip tip above estimated30.8 m loggia;its small lantern/finial37.5 m is estimated. Floor0.55 m,door/rose/archbay/roof/chapel splits and part datums remain approximate.No independent dimension facts or horizontal rescale."
  },
